model.py is checked out with one functional patch: the SSLModel class.

Original SSLModel loaded a local wav2vec 2.0 XLSR (300M) checkpoint via
fairseq.checkpoint_utils.load_model_ensemble_and_task(['xlsr2_300m.pt']),
requiring fairseq to be installed from the pinned commit bundled in the
upstream repo (fairseq-a54021305d6b3c4c5959ac9395135f63202db8f1/).

That install path does not work with a current pip: fairseq 1.0.0a0 pins
omegaconf<2.1, and the omegaconf 2.0.x wheels on PyPI have malformed
metadata (`PyYAML (>=5.1.*)` is not a valid version specifier) that modern
pip rejects outright — confirmed by attempting both `pip install fairseq`
(PyPI sdist fails to build: missing fairseq/version.txt, a known long-
standing packaging bug) and an editable install from the vendored fairseq
source (dependency resolution failure on omegaconf). This is a widely
reported problem with pinned-era fairseq on modern Python/pip, not
specific to this project's environment.

Patch: SSLModel now loads facebook/wav2vec2-xls-r-300m via HuggingFace
transformers (Wav2Vec2Model) instead of fairseq. This is the same
underlying XLS-R architecture/pretraining lineage, with matching
hidden_size=1024 (verified against the original fairseq path's
self.out_dim = 1024, so the downstream nn.Linear(1024, 128) projection
and the rest of the AASIST back-end are unaffected). extract_feat()'s
input/output contract (waveform in, (batch, frames, 1024) features out)
is unchanged, so no other code in this file needed to change.

The AASIST back-end (GraphAttentionLayer, HtrgGraphAttentionLayer,
GraphPool, Residual_block, Model) is untouched vendored code — same
architecture as clovaai/aasist (also vendored separately in AASIST/),
by the same author group (Jee-weon Jung et al.).

New dependency introduced by this vendoring: transformers (replacing the
fairseq requirement). The pretrained facebook/wav2vec2-xls-r-300m weights
(~1.2GB) download automatically on first use via huggingface_hub.
